course: dictionary
lesson: 12036
title: Short forms with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «CI» is an abbreviation, a short form of longer words. Capital letters often mean a shortened name or phrase, and one short form can stand for several different things. The words around it are the context, and they tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «The CI arrived at the crime scene and asked the officers for their notes.» Police words like crime scene and officers are the clues, so CI must mean Chief Inspector, a senior police officer.
explain: «The report said the average was 50, with a CI of 48 to 52.» Numbers and a range are the clues here. In science and maths, CI means confidence interval, a range of numbers that probably contains the true value.
explain: «The ferry to the CI leaves at noon, so pack your bags.» A ferry is a boat, and islands need ferries, so CI here means the Channel Islands. Always ask what would fit, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: CI is an abbreviation, a short form of longer words or phrases.
fact: CI can mean Chief Inspector, a senior police officer in the UK.
fact: In science and maths, CI means confidence interval: a range of numbers that probably contains the true value.
fact: CI is also a short form for the Channel Islands, and it is the code for Côte d'Ivoire.
fact: In Mandarin, «cì» means time, as in yí cì, once, and «cí» means word. «Cì» sounds like «tsuh».
exercise: «The CI checked the evidence at the station.» What does CI most likely mean here? | *Chief Inspector | Confidence interval | Channel Islands | Côte d'Ivoire
exercise: «The result was 12, with a CI from 10 to 14.» What does CI mean here? | Côte d'Ivoire | *Confidence interval | Channel Islands | Chief Inspector
exercise: In Mandarin, «yí cì» means once. What does «cì» mean here? | Island | Word | *Time | Police officer
test: «The CI is in charge of the case, and she wants the team at the station by nine.» What does CI mean? | *Chief Inspector | Channel Islands | Côte d'Ivoire | Confidence interval
test: «The survey gave an average of 40, with a CI of 37 to 43.» What does CI mean? | *Confidence interval | Côte d'Ivoire | Channel Islands | Chief Inspector
exam: «Dad says the ferry to the CI leaves at noon, so we need to pack.» Which meaning fits best? | Confidence interval | *Channel Islands | Mandarin word for time | Chief Inspector
